    <h1>New Age, Celtic, ambient and ethereal music: artists like Enya</h1>

<p><strong>New Age music</strong> emerged during the late 1960s and 1970s across Europe and the United States. It functions as a broad umbrella style designed to encourage relaxation, optimism, and artistic inspiration.</p>

<p>While often associated with spiritual movements or environmentalism, many famous artists reject these labels entirely. <strong>Enya</strong> identifies as Roman Catholic and maintains her music has no connection to New Age spirituality.</p>

<p>The music industry eventually formalized the genre's status. The <strong>Grammy Awards</strong> established strict criteria for the category, requiring albums to contain at least 51% newly recorded instrumental or vocal material.</p>

<h2>New Age Origins and Evolution</h2>

<p>Early pioneers laid the groundwork by combining acoustic instruments with non-traditional recording techniques. <strong>Tony Scott's</strong> 1964 album <em>Music for Zen Meditation</em> and <strong>Steven Halpern's</strong> 1975 release <em>Spectrum Suite</em> are foundational texts.</p>

<p>In 1969, <strong>Irv Teibel</strong> released his <em>Environments</em> series, which pioneered the use of psychoacoustic natural soundscapes. These early experiments blended seamlessly into the electronic synthesizer movements of the 1980s.</p>

<h3>Characteristics</h3>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Therapeutic atmosphere:</strong> Evokes serenity for <strong>yoga</strong>, <strong>massage</strong>, and <strong>meditation</strong>, focusing on stress management rather than a hypnotic trance state.</li>
  <li><strong>Diverse instrumentation:</strong> Blends acoustic flutes, harp, and piano with sustained <strong>synth pads</strong> and long <strong>sequencer</strong> runs.</li>
  <li><strong>Sonic fusion:</strong> Journalist <strong>Steven Rea</strong> described the genre as an acoustic and electronic mix incorporating jazz, folk, classical, and Eastern influences.</li>
  <li><strong>Natural elements:</strong> Frequently incorporates field recordings of falling rain, ocean waves, or animal calls directly into the musical arrangement.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Key New Age Artists</h3>

<p>A broad spectrum of pioneering soloists and composers define the movement across different eras:</p>

<ul>
